From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:22:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zink: acquire a swapchain resolve target before the batch
 uses it

begin_rendering's inlined-resolve path marked a swapchain resolve
target used by the batch before it acquired the target's image.
zink_batch_resource_usage_set then took the batch's acquire semaphore
from swapchain->images[dt_idx] with dt_idx still UINT32_MAX when the
window had a new swapchain and no image was acquired yet, and read far
outside the image array. The colour attachments' path
(prep_fb_attachment) acquires first; the resolve path now does too.

On an A19 Pro (KosmicKrisp) a 4x multisampled GL window made current
again after another window had held its layer crashed at its next swap
(begin_rendering -> zink_batch_rp -> kopperSwapBuffersWithDamage), and
windowed Counter-Strike on its OpenGL renderer faulted at the same
instruction; with the fault delivered to the game, the next swap waited
forever on the window system's lock the faulting one held.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-zink-followups.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c | 15 +++++++++------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
index e68869e..aae987d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
@@ -3473,6 +3473,15 @@ begin_rendering(struct zink_context *ctx, bool check_attachment_shadow)
             zink_resource_reference(&ctx->fb_resolve[i], NULL);
             continue;
          }
+         /* a swapchain resolve target is acquired before the batch uses it:
+          * the batch's acquire semaphore is the acquired image's
+          */
+         if (zink_is_swapchain(res)) {
+            if (!zink_kopper_acquire(ctx, res, UINT64_MAX)) {
+               zink_resource_reference(&ctx->fb_resolve[i], NULL);
+               return 0;
+            }
+         }
          zink_batch_resource_usage_set(ctx->bs, res, true, false);
          bool is_depth = util_format_is_depth_or_stencil(res->base.b.format);
          enum pipe_format format = res->base.b.format;
@@ -3487,12 +3496,6 @@ begin_rendering(struct zink_context *ctx, bool check_attachment_shadow)
             .first_layer = ctx->dynamic_fb.tc_info.resolve_geometry.z,
             .last_layer = ctx->dynamic_fb.tc_info.resolve_geometry.depth - 1,
          };
-         if (zink_is_swapchain(res)) {
-            if (!zink_kopper_acquire(ctx, res, UINT64_MAX)) {
-               zink_resource_reference(&ctx->fb_resolve[i], NULL);
-               return 0;
-            }
-         }
          VkImageViewCreateInfo ivci = create_ivci(screen, res, &tmpl, ctx->dynamic_fb.info.layerCount > 1 ? PIPE_TEXTURE_2D_ARRAY : PIPE_TEXTURE_2D);
          struct zink_surface *surf = zink_get_surface(ctx, &tmpl, &ivci);
          VkImageLayout layout = is_depth ? VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL : VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL;
-- 
2.55.0

